  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: jwcrypto 1.0+rhlw.1",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released jwcrypto 1.0+rhlw.1 with backported fixes for CVE-2022-3102, CVE-2024-28102, CVE-2026-39373, and CVE-2023-6681.\n\nCVE-2024-28102: JWCrypto vulnerable to JWT bomb Attack in `deserialize` function\n\nCVE-2026-39373: JWCrypto: JWE ZIP decompression bomb\n\nCVE-2023-6681: Jwcrypto: denail of service  via specifically crafted jwe\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for jwcrypto 1.0 from PyPI.",
